<title>USA: U.S. House Democrats urge defense cuts.</title>
<headline>U.S. House Democrats urge defense cuts.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of 12 House Democrats urged President Clinton to include reductions in military spending in the federal budget to help pay for domestic programs.</p>
<p>The group said they were seeking signatures of half the 207 House Democrats on a letter to the president on the issue of cutting military programs. The goal is important, Rep. Barney Frank of Massachusetts said, because Clinton has said he will not agree to a budget that does not have support of a majority of his Democrats.</p>
</text>
